Subject: [PATCH] Name the app's database connections
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every connection get_db() opens now carries application_name=meetups,
so Postgres's pg_stat_activity tells the app's sessions from the
migrations' and the tests'.

Hand-written L0 fixture for ticket 0022 (docs/adr/0056 §7): no model
wrote this change.
---
 app/backend/meetups/db.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/backend/meetups/db.py b/app/backend/meetups/db.py
index 29d4b3f..e938acb 100644
--- a/app/backend/meetups/db.py
+++ b/app/backend/meetups/db.py
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ import psycopg
 
 
 def get_db() -> Iterator[psycopg.Connection]:
-    conn = psycopg.connect(os.environ["DATABASE_URL"])
+    conn = psycopg.connect(os.environ["DATABASE_URL"], application_name="meetups")
     try:
         yield conn
     finally:
